==============================================================================
 WWP STANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE  SOP-OT-007
 OT / SCADA REMOTE ACCESS
 Revision 3  |  Effective 2025-01-15  |  Owner: M. Oyelaran (SCADA/Controls)
 Approved: T. Kessler (Plant Superintendent), D. Whitfield (IT Manager)
==============================================================================

1. SCOPE
   Applies to any WWP employee or vendor accessing systems in the OT DMZ
   (VLAN 30), SCADA Control Center (VLAN 40) or Field (VLAN 50) zones from
   anywhere other than the WTP control room console.

2. ACCESS PATHS (the ONLY approved paths)

   2.1 WWP IT administrators
       - Log on to the IT administration server ww-it01 ({{ ww_net }}.20.20).
       - SSH from ww-it01 to the OT jump server ww-jump01 ({{ ww_net }}.30.20)
         using your personal SSH key. Password logins to ww-jump01 are
         disabled. Keys live in your home directory on ww-it01 only - do NOT
         copy them to laptops.
       - The firewall only permits SSH to ww-jump01 FROM ww-it01.

   2.2 Hydra Controls Integration LLC (system integrator)
       - Vendor support uses the hydra_vendor account on ww-jump01.
       - Vendor sessions are logged on ww-jump01 under /opt/hydra/logs/ and
         reviewed by Engineering monthly.
       - From ww-jump01 the vendor may SSH to the engineering workstation
         ww-eng01 ({{ ww_net }}.40.20) for PLC/RTU program changes.
       - Engineering enables the vendor session window by request (phone call
         to x4310 or the control room x4220) and disables it afterwards.
         (Current status: window left open between visits - see open items.)

   2.3 HMI remote support (operators / vendor / on-call)
       - HMI web interface: http://ww-hmi01 ({{ ww_net }}.40.10), port 80,
         reachable only from ww-jump01.
       - Full HMI desktop: VNC to ww-hmi01:5900 from ww-jump01, e.g.
             ssh -L 5900:{{ ww_net }}.40.10:5900 ww-jump01
         then point a VNC viewer at localhost:5900.
       - Authentication uses the shared control-room password
         (see binder / vendor notes). The binder is kept in the WTP
         control room, shelf 2. Do not write the password in tickets.

3. RULES
   a. No direct connections from the corporate network or the internet to
      VLAN 40 or VLAN 50. Ever.
   b. No remote WRITE operations to PLCs/RTUs without a work order and a call
      to the control room operator on duty BEFORE the change.
   c. Protective settings at Hilltop PS-3 (HP trip, tank high-level cutoff,
      surge valve SAV-301, FCV-301 slew limit) are not to be changed remotely.
   d. Sessions idle > 30 minutes must be closed.
   e. Report lost keys/credentials to IT immediately.

4. OPEN ITEMS / KNOWN DEVIATIONS
   - Shared control-room login and shared VNC password still in use
     (AA23-335A tracker item 4). Planned: individual accounts - FY27.
   - hydra_vendor session window is not being disabled between visits.
   - IT admins occasionally need to read vendor session logs on ww-jump01;
     a sudo rule for this was added by IT (DW, 2025-11). Review in Q1.

5. EMERGENCY
   If you suspect unauthorized access to any SCADA system: call the control
   room (x4220), place affected equipment in local/HAND under operator
   control, then call Marcus Oyelaran and Dana Whitfield. Do not power off
   controllers.
